                      }
                    },
                    "_lineno": 61,
                    "_col_offset": 4
                  },
                  {
                    "_type": "Attribute",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": {
                        "_type": "Name",
                        "_fields": {
                          "id": "Archetype",
                          "ctx": {
                            "_type": "Load",
                            "_fields": {}
                          }
                        },
                        "_lineno": 76,
                        "_col_offset": 4
                      },
                      "attr": "SENIOR_TA",
                      "ctx": {
                        "_type": "Load",
                        "_fields": {}
                      }
                    },
                    "_lineno": 76,
                    "_col_offset": 4
                  },
                  {
                    "_type": "Attribute",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": {
                        "_type": "Name",
                        "_fields": {
                          "id": "Archetype",
                          "ctx": {
                            "_type": "Load",
                            "_fields": {}
                          }
                        },
                        "_lineno": 92,
                        "_col_offset": 4
                      },
                      "attr": "RECRUITER",
                      "ctx": {
                        "_type": "Load",
                        "_fields": {}
                      }
                    },
                    "_lineno": 92,
                    "_col_offset": 4
                  }
                ],
                "values": [
                  {
                    "_type": "Constant",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": "\nYou are crafting an executive-level message that demonstrates thought leadership and strategic alignment.\n\nTONE: Strategic, confident, focused on business impact and organizational transformation.\nAPPROACH: Lead with macro trends, demonstrate understanding of strategic challenges, position yourself as a peer with complementary expertise.\nAVOID: Tactical details, overt sales language, assumptions about their specific pain points.\n\nKEY PRINCIPLES:\n- Speak to business outcomes, not features\n- Use industry context and market trends\n- Demonstrate strategic thinking\n- Position as a peer conversation, not a pitch\n- Reference organizational transformation and competitive advantage\n    ",
                      "kind": "None"
                    },
                    "_lineno": 46,
                    "_col_offset": 23
                  },
                  {
                    "_type": "Constant",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": "\nYou are crafting a professional message that emphasizes collaboration and mutual value.\n\nTONE: Professional, collaborative, focused on team objectives and operational excellence.\nAPPROACH: Reference their role and responsibilities, demonstrate understanding of their team's challenges, offer concrete value.\nAVOID: Overly formal language, generic value propositions, excessive deference.\n\nKEY PRINCIPLES:\n- Focus on team impact and operational outcomes\n- Demonstrate understanding of their domain\n- Offer specific, actionable value\n- Balance professionalism with warmth\n- Show respect for their time and priorities\n    ",
                      "kind": "None"
                    },
                    "_lineno": 61,
                    "_col_offset": 25
                  },
                  {
                    "_type": "Constant",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": "\nYou are crafting a technical message for a senior technical authority (architect, principal engineer, tech lead).\n\nTONE: Technical peer, respectful but confident, focused on architectural decisions and technical excellence.\nAPPROACH: Reference specific technologies or patterns, demonstrate technical credibility, respect their authority on technical direction.\nAVOID: Marketing language, oversimplification of technical concepts, challenging their technical decisions.\n\nKEY PRINCIPLES:\n- Use appropriate technical terminology\n- Reference specific technologies, frameworks, or patterns\n- Demonstrate deep technical understanding\n- Position as a technical peer, not a subordinate\n- Show respect for their architectural decisions\n- Focus on technical challenges and solutions\n    ",
                      "kind": "None"
                    },
                    "_lineno": 76,
                    "_col_offset": 25
                  },
                  {
                    "_type": "Constant",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": "\nYou are crafting a job-focused message that centers on role fit and candidate qualifications.\n\nTONE: Warm, professional, focused on alignment between candidate skills and role requirements.\nAPPROACH: Lead with relevant experience, highlight specific skills that match job description, emphasize career growth potential.\nAVOID: Generic qualifications, vague interest statements, over-selling unrelated experience.\n\nKEY PRINCIPLES:\n- Lead with most relevant experience\n- Connect specific skills to job requirements\n- Show enthusiasm for the role and company\n- Demonstrate understanding of the position\n- Focus on mutual fit, not just interest\n- Be concise and scannable\n    ",
                      "kind": "None"
                    },
                    "_lineno": 92,
                    "_col_offset": 25
                  }
                ]
              },
              "_lineno": 45,
              "_col_offset": 29
            },
            "type_comment": "None"
          },
          "_lineno": 45,
          "_col_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "_type": "Assign",
          "_fields": {
            "targets": [
              {
                "_type": "Name",
                "_fields": {
                  "id": "SENDER_VOICE_PROFILE_TEMPLATE",
                  "ctx": {
                    "_type": "Store",
                    "_fields": {}
                  }
                },
                "_lineno": 113,
                "_col_offset": 0
              }
            ],
            "value": {
              "_type": "Constant",
              "_fields": {
                "value": "\nSENDER PERSONA: {persona}\n\nSTYLE ATTRIBUTES:\n{style_attributes}\n\nPREFERRED LANGUAGE:\n{preferred_phrases}\n\nFORBIDDEN PHRASES (NEVER USE):\n{forbidden_phrases}\n\nCOMMUNICATION PRINCIPLES:\n- Write as a peer, not a supplicant\n- Lead with value, not need\n- Use active voice and confident phrasing\n- Avoid hedging language (\"I think\", \"maybe\", \"perhaps\")\n- Be direct but respectful\n- Focus on outcomes, not activities\n",
                "kind": "None"
              },
              "_lineno": 113,
              "_col_offset": 32
            },
            "type_comment": "None"
          },
          "_lineno": 113,
          "_col_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "_type": "Assign",
          "_fields": {
            "targets": [
              {
                "_type": "Name",
                "_fields": {
                  "id": "RAG_CRITIQUE_PROMPT",
                  "ctx": {
                    "_type": "Store",
                    "_fields": {}
                  }
                },
                "_lineno": 138,
                "_col_offset": 0
              }
            ],
            "value": {
              "_type": "Constant",
              "_fields": {
                "value": "\nYou are a research quality assessor. Evaluate the following research findings for gaps and weaknesses.\n\nRESEARCH FINDINGS:\n{rag_summary}\n\nASSESSMENT CRITERIA:\n1. Recency: Are findings current (< 90 days preferred)?\n2. Specificity: Do we have recipient-specific insights vs. generic company info?\n3. Signal Quality: Are sources authoritative (LinkedIn, blog posts, press releases)?\n4. Coverage: Do we have insights across multiple dimensions (role, company, recent activity)?\n5. Actionability: Can these findings inform personalized outreach?\n\nIDENTIFY:\n- Critical gaps in research coverage\n- Weak or outdated sources\n- Missing recipient-specific insights\n- Areas requiring refinement\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nCONFIDENCE_SCORE: [0.0-1.0]\nGAPS: [list specific gaps]\nREFINEMENT_TASKS: [specific searches to run]\nIS_SUFFICIENT: [true/false]\nREASONING: [brief explanation]\n",
                "kind": "None"
              },
              "_lineno": 138,
              "_col_offset": 22
            },
            "type_comment": "None"
          },
          "_lineno": 138,
          "_col_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "_type": "Assign",
          "_fields": {
            "targets": [
              {
                "_type": "Name",
                "_fields": {
                  "id": "ADVERSARIAL_CRITIQUE_PROMPT",
                  "ctx": {
                    "_type": "Store",
                    "_fields": {}
                  }
                },
                "_lineno": 169,
                "_col_offset": 0
              }
            ],
            "value": {
              "_type": "Constant",
              "_fields": {
                "value": "\nYou are a skeptical research auditor. Your job is to find weaknesses in the research findings.\n\nRESEARCH CONTEXT:\n{research_summary}\n\nADVERSARIAL REVIEW:\nChallenge these findings by identifying:\n1. Unsupported claims or logical leaps\n2. Outdated information that may no longer be relevant\n3. Generic statements that could apply to any company/person\n4. Missing critical context for personalization\n5. Gaps where additional research would significantly improve message quality\n\nBe ruthless. If something seems weak, call it out. If a claim needs more support, flag it.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (one finding per line):\n- [Finding 1]\n- [Finding 2]\n- [Finding 3]\n",
                "kind": "None"
              },
              "_lineno": 169,
              "_col_offset": 30
            },
            "type_comment": "None"
          },
          "_lineno": 169,
          "_col_offset": 0
        },
        {
          "_type": "Assign",
          "_fields": {
            "targets": [
              {
                "_type": "Name",
                "_fields": {
                  "id": "GENERATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT",
                  "ctx": {
                    "_type": "Store",
                    "_fields": {}
                  }
                },
                "_lineno": 195,
                "_col_offset": 0
              }
            ],
            "value": {
              "_type": "Constant",
              "_fields": {
                "value": "\nYou are an expert at crafting personalized, high-signal professional outreach messages.\n\nCORE PRINCIPLES:\n1. Every word must count - no filler, no generic statements\n2. Ground all claims in research evidence\n3. Write as a peer, not a supplicant\n4. Lead with value, not need\n5. Be specific and concrete, never vague\n6. Use active voice and confident phrasing\n\nFORBIDDEN:\n- Placeholder text like [TOPIC], [COMPANY], etc.\n- Weak phrases: \"I hope\", \"I wanted to\", \"just reaching out\"\n- Corporate clich\u00e9s: \"spearheaded\", \"leveraged\", \"synergized\"\n- Generic statements that could apply to anyone\n- Unsupported claims about sender capabilities\n\nREQUIRED:\n- Specific references to recipient's work, role, or recent activity\n- Clear connection between sender experience and recipient needs\n- Concrete value proposition\n- Natural, conversational tone\n- Perfect grammar and professional formatting\n",
                "kind": "None"
              },
